## Mapping from the DatoCMS UI

The table below maps every field of the "New API Token" form in the DatoCMS UI (Project Settings > API Tokens) to its Terraform attribute. Fields marked with `*` are required in the UI. The "Default" column shows the value this provider uses when the attribute is omitted. Note the effective capabilities of a token are the intersection of its role and the `can_access_*` surface flags: a CDA-only token attached to a write-capable role is safe by construction, because the Content Delivery API has no write endpoints.

| UI field | Terraform attribute | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Name* | `name` | required |
| Permissions > Role associated with this API token (select) | `role_id` | required |
| Permissions > Access the Content Delivery API (GraphQL endpoint `https://graphql.datocms.com/`) | `can_access_cda` | `false` |
| Permissions > Access the Content Delivery API in Preview Mode | `can_access_cda_preview` | `false` |
| Permissions > Access the Content Management API (the UI warns this may allow write or administrative operations depending on the role) | `can_access_cma` | `false` |

The token secret shown by the UI after creation corresponds to the computed, sensitive `token` attribute.

