## Import

Import is supported using the access token ID:

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Note: on import the `token` secret is populated only if the API token used by the provider belongs to a role with `can_manage_access_tokens`; otherwise the API masks it (returns null) and the attribute stays empty in the state until a read with sufficient permissions happens.

## Deletion and rotation notes

- If the token owns resources (records, uploads, filters, editing sessions), the DatoCMS API refuses a plain delete and requires transferring ownership first (query parameters `destination_user_type`/`destination_user_id`, not modeled by this resource); in that case the destroy fails with an explanatory API error.
- A token cannot delete itself: destroying the very token the provider is authenticated with fails with `CANNOT_DESTROY_CURRENT_USER`.
- Secret rotation is a separate API endpoint (POST `/access_tokens/{id}/regenerate_token`) and is not managed by this resource. After an out-of-band rotation, run a refresh to store the new secret.
